1. लिह् (later form of √ रिह्) cl. 2. P. Ā. (Dhātup. xxiv, 6) लेढि, लीढे (ep. also लिहति; pf. लिलेह, लिलिहे Gr.; fut. लेढा, लेक्ष्यति, ˚ते, ib.; aor. अलिक्षत्, अलिक्षत and अलीढ, ib.; inf. लेढुम्, ib.; ind.p. लीढ्वा, ib.)
to lick, lap, lick at (loc.), taste, sip, take any food by licking or lapping, Br. &c. &c.;
to lick up = destroy (said of an arrow), Daś.;
 Caus. लेह॑यति (aor. अलीलिहत्), to cause to lick, Br.; Suśr.;
to apply as an electuary, Car. :
Desid. लिलिक्षति, ˚ते Gr.:
Intens. लेलिह्यति, लेलेढि (p. लेलिहत्, ˚ह्यत्, ˚ह्यमन or ˚हान, q.v.), to lick frequently or constantly, play with the tongue, MBh.; R. &c.
